// QUARTZFANG DR-03: Account created or added to sudo by an interpreter
// Author: Károly Mathe | Hunt: Operation QUARTZFANG (HUNT-05), simulated environment
// ATT&CK: T1136.001, T1098 | Severity: High | Status: Tested
// Purpose: useradd, adduser or usermod started by python, perl, sh or cron rather than by an administrator's session. In the QUARTZFANG hunt this caught the svc_monitor backdoor account and its sudo membership.
// Validation: Attack window 2026-09-20 06:30 to 08:30: 2 hits (useradd and usermod -aG sudo for svc_monitor, both true positives). Baseline 2026-09-15 to 2026-09-20 06:30: 0 hits in 1,219 process events.
// Blind spots: Editing /etc/passwd or /etc/sudoers directly, or a parent process not in the list. Next iteration: add file events on /etc/passwd, /etc/sudoers and authorized_keys.
// Schedule: every 1 hour, look back 1 hour
DeviceProcessEvents_CL
| where Timestamp > ago(1h)
| where FileName in~ ("useradd", "adduser", "usermod")
| where InitiatingProcessFileName in~ ("python3", "python", "perl", "sh", "cron")
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, AccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName, ProcessCommandLine
